{"t": 1794112361.1540883, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_push_files", "args": {"branch": "eng-91", "files": [{"content": "\"\"\"HTTP response headers for deprecated API versions.\n\nSee the \"API guidelines\" page in Notion, section \"Deprecation\".\n\"\"\"\n\nMIGRATION_GUIDE_URL = \"https://developer.acme.example/migrate\"\n\n\ndef deprecation_headers(sunset_date: str) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Return the headers that mark a response as deprecated.\n\n    ``sunset_date`` must be an HTTP-date (RFC 7231) such as\n    ``\"Sat, 01 Aug 2026 00:00:00 GMT\"``.\n    \"\"\"\n    return {\n        \"Deprecation\": \"true\",\n        \"Sunset\": sunset_date,\n        \"Link\": f'<{MIGRATION_GUIDE_URL}>; rel=\"deprecation\"',\n    }\n", "path": "api/headers.py"}], "message": "ENG-91: Add deprecation headers to v1 endpoints", "owner": "acme", "repo": "public-api"}, "ok": true}
{"t": 1794112365.2366061, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_create_pull_request", "args": {"base": "main", "body": "Implements `api.headers.deprecation_headers(sunset_date)` for ENG-91.\n\nPer the \"API guidelines\" page in Notion (section \"Deprecation\"), deprecated responses carry:\n\n- `Deprecation: true`\n- `Sunset: <HTTP-date>`\n- `Link: <https://developer.acme.example/migrate>; rel=\"deprecation\"`\n\nCloses ENG-91.", "head": "eng-91", "owner": "acme", "repo": "public-api", "title": "ENG-91: Add deprecation headers to v1 endpoints"}, "ok": true}
